menu "WHM Bring-up Configuration"

    config WHM_WIFI_SSID
        string "WiFi SSID (STA mode; leave empty for SoftAP mode)"
        default ""
        help
            If set, the board joins this network as a station and its TSF
            clock disciplines to that AP's beacons. If empty, the board
            starts its own SoftAP (see WHM_SOFTAP_SSID) and becomes the
            beacon source - the off-grid conductor topology.

    config WHM_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "WiFi password (STA mode)"
        default ""

    config WHM_SOFTAP_SSID
        string "SoftAP SSID (used when WHM_WIFI_SSID is empty)"
        default "WHM-BRINGUP"

    config WHM_SOFTAP_PASSWORD
        string "SoftAP password (>= 8 chars for WPA2, empty for open)"
        default "whitehat-matrix"

    config WHM_RUN_AUDIO_TEST
        bool "Run speaker tone + microphone RMS test at boot"
        default y
        help
            Plays a 1kHz burst through the ES8311/speaker path and captures
            1s from the ES7210 dual mics, logging per-channel RMS and peak.
            Disable if no speaker is connected and you want a quiet bench.

    config WHM_TEST_BRIGHTNESS
        int "Display test brightness (0-255)"
        range 10 255
        default 100
        help
            Applied at display init. The solid-white pattern at 255 can pull
            ~4A on a 64x64 P2.5 panel; 100 keeps bring-up polite to small
            bench supplies. Raise once your power budget is verified.

endmenu
